All 320 released Base text tensors were bit-identical to the native loader's 752,393,024 parameters before quantization. The ordinary and recurrent views shared all 680 frozen array objects after conversion (817,093,312 bytes). The fit saw 102,827 response tokens in 270.64 optimizer seconds after 209.48 s of prefix preparation. A fresh research wheel built twice identically and ran outside the source checkout. On a new print-shop question with independently computed answer 704, both decoders exhausted 384 tokens before returning a quantity. A second standalone invocation reproduced the candidate's entire trace.

== Changing the question while keeping the evidence fixed

A receipt-review model can learn to reject implausible calculations even when it has trouble choosing the right calculation for a user. We therefore enrolled paired questions with the same evidence and different correct answers. There are 256 distinct SQuAD training paragraphs, each with two original human questions and different numeric answers. We also aligned 44 SVAMP story pairs on the same quantities. The human question wording was retained. We evaluated each original equation against its publisher answer, substituted the aligned numbers, executed both expressions again and kept pairs with numerically different returns. Each calculation serves as a correct response to one question and an incorrect response to the other. This balances the surface form of the expressions across the two roles.

The new adapters start from the pinned instruction sibling with a groupwise eight-bit prefix. Both applications of the final native layer share the rank-32 parameters and each owns its own cache. The model learns to emit an opening call, answer after a correct return, revise the other question's calculation, and complete the revision. Alongside 640 prior action and response records, training contains 1,504 supervised turns. Each of 960 AdamW updates draws two complete pairs and four individual turns. The objective adds a contrastive term to ordinary response cross-entropy. At the first divergent target token the contrastive term rewards a shift of at least one logit in the relative margin for the two labels when the user changes the question. Cross-entropy separately supervises each whole target response.

We held the entire DROP corpus out of fitting. Its independent development annotations select two differently answered numeric questions about each of 24 passages [60]. Every included reference agrees with at least one additional human judgment and with every other recorded validation judgment. All 24 passage texts are distinct. Fifteen have history IDs and nine have football IDs. The publisher repeats the same Wikipedia URL on all 24 records, so we use passage IDs for grouping. The largest four-word-shingle Jaccard similarity between two enrolled passages is 0.125. Each model sees the complete passage and each question begins a new conversation. The primary unit is the passage: both original questions must receive correct completed answers. We also enrolled 24 fresh ASDiv questions, all 22 public numerical tools, and the 12 two-request local service conversations. Both models freely generated all their tokens with Qwen’s published interface, identical calculator access and a 384-token thinking-enabled allowance per turn. The 106 dialogues correspond to 118 user requests and 82 scoring clusters after grouping questions about the same DROP passage.

We also compared the local supervised user wording across sources. Removing the common answer-format instruction left 1,176 distinct unmasked training questions. None of the 48 held-out DROP or 24 ASDiv requests matched exactly. With numbers masked, the highest five-word Jaccard scores were 0.032 for DROP questions, 0.179 for ASDiv, and 0.114 for the 24 DROP passage bodies against the 256 SQuAD training passages. None crossed 0.6. These counts address overlap in the local fit; the original pretraining inventory is unavailable. The public function and service panels were retained from earlier evaluations and measure retention.

Across 960 updates, 802,816 trainable parameters received 151,461 response targets. Frozen-prefix preparation took 253.42 seconds and optimization took 419.30 seconds. The loop completed all 118 requests in 73.17 seconds; Base completed 91 in 513.29 seconds. Summed first-token time was 24.18 versus 22.39 seconds and peak allocation was 1.11 versus 1.70 GiB. Grouping the paired passage questions, the registered endpoint was 42/82 versus 33/82 with 14 gains and five losses ($p=0.0636$). Counting all 106 dialogues separately gave 44 versus 44.

On the 48 unseen DROP questions the loop supplied two correct numbers and Base thirteen. The loop answered both questions correctly on zero of 24 passages. Base did so on two. The loop never executed the calculator on DROP, then executed it on all 24 ASDiv questions. Twelve fresh ASDiv answers were correct and grounded, against nine grounded and fifteen correct final answers for Base. Asked how much a trade deficit increased, the loop answered “2015/2016 deficit: 1228 - 401” without evaluating it. Base returned 827. The training data associate passage questions with direct answers and word problems with calls. The observed action split is consistent with learning that association. It leaves open whether the same model can learn to select the action from the computation the user needs.

The paired training data perfectly associated source type with the opening action. The 512 SQuAD passage targets all supplied direct answers and all 88 paired SVAMP opening targets requested arithmetic. Held-out behavior repeated this division. On seven of 24 DROP passages the loop produced the same visible answer to both distinct questions. Base completed both answers on twelve passages and repeated none of those twelve. Of ten questions with the reference value literally printed as a decimal in the passage, the loop answered zero and Base three. Of 38 without that printed decimal, it answered two and Base ten. These counts describe actions and visible answers. The training design cannot isolate whether source, wording, supervision or another feature determined the action.

